[# decorative/star-rating: filled and empty stars for a rating out of 5, with an optional label ("4.9 out of 5").

   Stars are text glyphs (filled and outline), so they work without images. The rating is rounded to the nearest
   whole star. A screen reader reads the label, so always pass one for a real rating (the stars are marked
   aria-hidden).

   Compatibility
   - Outlook desktop: star glyphs render from the system symbol font.
   - Gmail apps: fine.
   - Dark mode: filled stars keep the star color, empty stars use the border color. #]
[% set full = data.rating | round(0) | int %]
<mj-text[[ cc(cls) ]] align="[[ s.align ]]" padding="[[ s.padding ]]">
  <span aria-hidden="true" style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:[[ s.size ]];letter-spacing:2px;line-height:1;color:[[ s.color ]];">[% for i in range(0, 5) %][% if i < full %]&#9733;[% else %]<span style="color:[[ s.emptyColor ]];">&#9733;</span>[% endif %][% endfor %]</span>
  [% if data.label %]<span style="[[ typoCss('bodySmall') ]]margin-left:6px;">[[ data.label ]]</span>[% endif %]
</mj-text>
